#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083007 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/id #uuid "e930a29a-6adf-5aaa-9b44-86dd8d570ae7" :question/math-academy-id "e-5354" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$4 y^2  - 10 x^2 - 8 y  - 40 x  = 76?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-10{x}^{2}-8y-40x & =76 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-8y-10{x}^{2}-40x & =76 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-2y]-10[{x}^{2}+4x] & =76 \\\\ 4[(y-1)^{2}-1]-10[(x+2)^{2}-4] & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-4-10(x+2)^{2}+40 & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =76-40+4 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =40 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-2,1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083078 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083297 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f99d4fec-bc58-5a09-9fac-38b46f233489" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola"}] :question/id #uuid "0caa1041-a564-5428-9838-20cea32fdf17" :question/math-academy-id "e-6775" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} - \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1 ?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k = 2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083079 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/id #uuid "8e31f5b5-ff87-5c45-b143-66dfdcb4ab8c" :question/math-academy-id "e-6776" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(y+3)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} = 1 ?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-(-3))^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083080 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/id #uuid "af591507-e248-53d2-a391-e053cdc3fdea" :question/math-academy-id "e-6777" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](images/5e/5e01d30ade2c26c6befcc21339aff858a2cfaaec406df7428cc9770d70903ce2.png)" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ![](images/2a/2ac743df1895cd3a2185fadc273945035e01ff93c9bda9394f6b37eeaeba7e7d.png) is given by\n![](images/81/813e411586523b884a123a4794c1cb06d7b95f675ca75e1b994c6b09c3fe6a92.png)\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group ![](images/d1/d158d97a9b8654a3178eaed05119d604b49295b63e914dc468153bfd7cea88bc.png) and ![](images/67/6752ce15229c41002c859a3e31d785189a80c096d49c3b85ab011d3ce9506d1c.png) terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n![](images/f5/f5e8733c3f7e629ea43c6e37f69f796f8fa66a88e10e978eb944a8ebc01e0009.png)\n\nTherefore, the center is ![](images/1c/1cbb0b8cf874096a80504a2f37e87f6b7ced32f3129a9e7e4ab0348753e91bfe.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e982ecf-50aa-5265-ab59-2a7cd50d4cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238602} {:answer/id #uuid "8a05fb7b-ff3d-59b6-ae7e-c48371bbd54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239257} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fe10d0-96f2-5ba4-98c4-144d00023311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239644} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f87bb8-2f3c-5c32-bdbf-781f71dbbb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239816} {:answer/id #uuid "fb7fe14e-1e8e-51e0-ba16-deb3767103f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7f87bb8-2f3c-5c32-bdbf-781f71dbbb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239816} :answer-field/id #uuid "616c37f6-578b-5c62-b4f2-9fbe2de0c631" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8da39e7-a362-5791-804a-eb37d095c286" :question/math-academy-id "q-10419" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x & =0 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-16y-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-4y]-[{x}^{2}-4x] & =0 \\\\ 4[(y-2)^{2}-4]-[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-16-(x-2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =16-4 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250524 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "316d7132-e4d2-552b-8229-76cf4a760b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247871} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9febdf-840d-5e4a-9454-270334fac866" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248674} {:answer/id #uuid "bb19e8fc-2e30-562b-bb53-409259921842" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249096} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb9b84b-92e1-5992-bbf6-9dbd59a7b2b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249366} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d8c934-c5fd-5811-a685-9aa2936725ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3d8c934-c5fd-5811-a685-9aa2936725ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249432} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb9b725b-1554-5fc4-b7bb-be67fcd944ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35bb8fc9-b273-5104-bbf5-373700e22296" :question/math-academy-id "q-116100" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{36}-\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{{6}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-1$ and $k=5.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-1,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "223e29c9-1bb5-51ee-9ec8-4d5c15363951" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Horizontal Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11296e99-5c2b-5793-8e8d-217c986ab5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247576} {:answer/id #uuid "17cf6d61-728d-5567-a591-e5c9861f362c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247639} {:answer/id #uuid "89bc0561-6cc5-51b9-8c4b-b00b6d2c71df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248647} {:answer/id #uuid "af45d168-87c9-589c-9752-0b7af98e294f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248995} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3d35d4-3130-5c40-b479-331fd076ff0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17cf6d61-728d-5567-a591-e5c9861f362c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247639} :answer-field/id #uuid "14dfe21a-85ac-5482-9b66-fe8a40beb6a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249704}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9369b477-cb7c-5149-8c85-5d42daef382f" :question/math-academy-id "q-116110" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$6{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+48x-48y=72?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}+48x-48y & =72 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}+48x-4{y}^{2}-48y & =72 \\\\ 6[{x}^{2}+8x]-4[{y}^{2}+12y] & =72 \\\\ 6[(x+4)^{2}-16]-4[(y+6)^{2}-36] & =72 \\\\ 6(x+4)^{2}-96-4(y+6)^{2}+144 & =72 \\\\ 6(x+4)^{2}-4(y+6)^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-(-6))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-4,-6).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0da8f012-4b8e-59d2-86f2-6cf9ded76584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247549} {:answer/id #uuid "1d73eb71-f3b0-5802-bd97-3518478f6143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247688} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6e6b00-01a7-50ba-8b49-1508e2c1ebb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248267} {:answer/id #uuid "93a15523-e8ae-509a-8f92-1e5d130afcfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248737} {:answer/id #uuid "f70239d3-779d-5762-a4c5-9498427f2ea9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c6e6b00-01a7-50ba-8b49-1508e2c1ebb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248267} :answer-field/id #uuid "465002b5-f411-5a4c-a8ea-09bf4dac334e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "09ea155c-8ce4-5cf1-a51e-cc7b1072dc21" :question/math-academy-id "q-116116" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola $6{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-60y+8x=-122?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-60y+8x & =-122 \\\\ 6{y}^{2}-60y-4{x}^{2}+8x & =-122 \\\\ 6[{y}^{2}-10y]-4[{x}^{2}-2x] & =-122 \\\\ 6[(y-5)^{2}-25]-4[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =-122 \\\\ 6(y-5)^{2}-150-4(x-1)^{2}+4 & =-122 \\\\ 6(y-5)^{2}-4(x-1)^{2} & =-122+150-4 \\\\ 6(y-5)^{2}-4(x-1)^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(1,5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250535 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a69e3eb-1241-510a-bcae-cbe4dc04cf6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247514} {:answer/id #uuid "25b693f8-50c5-55b9-8b7d-74edb833c772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247758} {:answer/id #uuid "4649358d-dcf0-5d38-97b3-76fefc264ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248053} {:answer/id #uuid "c7cea033-1dd5-57ca-871c-75a8897b745c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249202} {:answer/id #uuid "db6228aa-8413-55b3-ad06-6b02e28b361c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4649358d-dcf0-5d38-97b3-76fefc264ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248053} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e0bb405-9db2-5f8a-b20f-6371a2d3243f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c70eacd9-b18b-5a32-b727-b9fb2382ee5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-116123" :question/problem "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-10x+4y=31?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-10x+4y & =31 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}+4y-{x}^{2}-10x & =31 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}+2y]-[{x}^{2}+10x] & =31 \\\\ 2[(y+1)^{2}-1]-[(x+5)^{2}-25] & =31 \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-2-(x+5)^{2}+25 & =31 \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-(x+5)^{2} & =31+2-25 \\\\ 2(y+1)^{2}-(x+5)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-5))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{8})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-5,-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e8ee273-4732-5670-8aa8-65f3d5e4951b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e8ee273-4732-5670-8aa8-65f3d5e4951b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300012} :answer-field/id #uuid "89ea00a3-33b5-51ed-b336-09e167ef7f23" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd6f5969-e632-5bb1-94fb-b3769aafecf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd6f5969-e632-5bb1-94fb-b3769aafecf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301058} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7b8c08b-235a-5816-8d85-e9b012a94ace" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a38cb36d-c0e0-5001-b269-6ab08e9aaaff" :question/math-academy-id "q-328317" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{81}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{9}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=3$ and $k=0.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,0\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "345d6df7-2ada-5c2e-8146-7c779afae3af" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a Vertical Hyperbola Given an Equation in Expanded Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5810b4-ca85-5c7e-a9fc-58e4df87a7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a5810b4-ca85-5c7e-a9fc-58e4df87a7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300243} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2a5382-ea17-5843-a92f-c7df2fb5dccd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2bfcc51-e77e-5489-87c0-5d48b98f06f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2bfcc51-e77e-5489-87c0-5d48b98f06f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301159} :answer-field/id #uuid "48e25f6e-a392-562d-9f6e-ba45ff4f97d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "937b8770-6fd6-5e2a-a6a3-e0d265d81c6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-328401" :question/problem "The center of the hyperbola $16{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}+96y=256$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{y}^{2}-25{x}^{2}+96y & =256 \\\\ 16{y}^{2}+96y\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16[{y}^{2}+6y]\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16[(y+3)^{2}-9]\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16(y+3)^{2}-144\\,-\\,25{x}^{2} & =256 \\\\ 16(y+3)^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =256+144 \\\\ 16(y+3)^{2}-25{x}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,-3\\,).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083298 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdab0134-e416-51cf-89fa-73ad4a2c2eb9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center of a V